    888	| §P.P2 batched π_h(x) on h, slot 2 — does the within-window cross-x ensemble of HL residuals r_h(x) = π_h(x) − S_h·li_2(x) at fixed (anchor, h) follow a half-Gaussian shape (Thread 7 slot 2 transposition); is there a stable F_GUE-like factor σ_eff/σ_pred? | EXPERIMENT (B-MIXED: cross-x within-window FAILS half-Gaussian KS due to random-walk-like correlation; cross-h at fixed x PASSES with median KS p ≈ 0.7-0.8; σ-suppression ratio in [0.36, 0.70] but NOT decade-stable like Thread 7's F_GUE = 0.755) | E (E1.5 + S195 + S224 + S240..S244 + S418 — methodological finding identifies cross-h as the natural ensemble for HL residual analysis; refines slot-1 dichotomy into ensemble-aware form) | Thread 8 commit step 2/4 (S419). Built `experiments/analytic/batched_pi_h/slot2_multisample.py` (~340 lines): batched-sieve via numpy AND-shift cumsum (memory-efficient; 720 rows in 21s total wall time). Three anchors x ∈ {10⁶, 10⁷, 10⁸} × N=30 log-uniform x_j in quarter-decade [x_anchor, x_anchor·10^{0.25}] × 8 representative h ∈ {2, 6, 14, 22, 30, 42, 90, 198} (S_h ∈ [1.32, 4.0]). Three statistical aggregates: (A) per-(anchor, h) cross-x KS (24 cells, N=30 each); (B) per-(anchor, x_j) cross-h KS (90 cells, N=8 each); (C) pooled per-anchor (N=240 each). **Headline finding**: cross-x at fixed (anchor, h) FAILS half-Gaussian KS — median p_eff = 0.033, only 8/24 cells with p > 0.1. Cells that fail show median/σ_eff ≈ mean/σ_eff ≈ 0.95 (theoretical half-Gaussian = 0.6745/0.7979) — clustered |r| values, not Gaussian-tailed. Within-window range diagnostic: (max|r| − min|r|)/σ_eff has mean ≈ 1.5 across cells; residuals drift but don't decohere. **Structural diagnosis**: HL_h(x) = S_h · li_2(x) is analytic-smooth, π_h(x) is step; the residual is a slowly-varying random-walk in x (drift O(σ_eff) within quarter-decade, no oscillation), unlike Thread 7's zero-truncation residual which oscillates with wavelength ~1/log x. Cross-x sampling within a small log-window does NOT give iid samples for HL residuals. **Cross-h at fixed (anchor, x_j) PASSES half-Gaussian KS**: median p_eff = 0.840 / 0.698 / 0.804 at anchors 10⁶/10⁷/10⁸; **all 90/90 cells with p > 0.1**. The cross-h ensemble is the natural sampling for HL residual shape analysis. **σ-suppression ratio σ_eff/σ_pred_pois = 0.36-0.70** across 24 (anchor, h) cells, where σ_pred_pois = √(S_h·li_2(x)) is the HL random-residual Poisson prediction. Empirical RMS is consistently SMALLER than Poisson — analogue of Thread 7's GUE pair-correlation suppression (correlations among primes via singular series itself reduce the variance below random-residual). NOT decade-stable: 0.50 → 0.70 → 0.41 across 10⁶/10⁷/10⁸; the 10⁷ bump driven by anomaly cell (10⁷, h=6) cousin-prime σ_eff/σ_pois = 1.64 (signed range = 481, persistent large residual episode). Excluding h=6: ratio narrows to ~0.36-0.43, still mildly drifting with x. **Pooled per-anchor (N=240) KS**: borderline at 10⁶ (p=0.082), reject at 10⁷ (p<0.001, h=6 outlier), borderline at 10⁸ (p=0.217). Half-Gaussian shape holds at the cell level but pooled hides the anomaly. **What this rules out**: (i) the original Thread-7-direct-transposition hypothesis "HL has stable F_GUE-like σ_eff/σ_pred ≈ 0.74 across decades" — directly tested, ratio drifts in [0.36, 0.70]; (ii) cross-x sampling within quarter-decade as a fair iid ensemble for HL residual statistics — methodologically rejected. **What this does NOT close**: (i) cross-h ensemble at fixed x as a path to a precise σ-formula for HL — slot 2 demonstrates shape but does not derive σ_eff(x, h) closed form; (ii) Q-truncated singular series cost-vs-error tradeoff — slot 3; (iii) anchor extension to 10⁹/10¹⁰ to test whether σ_eff/σ_pois stabilises — slot 3 side measurement; (iv) named-exponent error bound for polylog HL evaluator — slot 3-4 wrap. **Methodological warning** (preserved for slot 3+ design): within-window cross-x sampling is misleading for HL residual analysis; use cross-h at fixed x. **Cross-domain