st Q with σ_HL_Q ≤ 1.05·σ_HL_∞. **Sharp half-Gaussian shape transition Q=100 → Q=200**: cross-h KS median p_eff jumps from 0.0015 (Q=100, 0/10 cells pass p>0.1) to 0.96 (Q=200, 10/10 cells pass), tracking the σ-knee. Below the knee, truncation contamination dominates intrinsic noise and breaks the slot-2 half-Gaussian profile; above the knee, cross-h shape recovers across all 10 cells. **σ_HL_Q values across (anchor, x_j, Q)**: at x=10⁷, σ drops from 638→446→357→174→168→171→172→173→173 across Q={30, 50, 100, 200, 500, 1000, 2000, 5000, ∞}; at x=10⁸, 5163→3615→2996→528→441→419→405→409→409. Plateau at Q ≥ 2000 (all max_p_h in our set ≤ 2003). **Per-h cost dimension**: S_Q(h) by trial division costs min(Q, √h) odd integers tested. For h_max=4006, full S_∞ is 31 steps, Q=30 is 15 steps (50% saving). Average cost across 26-h ensemble: 7.0 (Q=30) → 8.5 (Q=∞), 18% saving. **Q-truncation gives no asymptotic cost saving in original P2 polylog regime** (h ≤ poly log x ⇒ √h ≤ poly log x ≤ Q* = √x/log x); knee Q* is *algebraic* in x, not polylog. **What this rules out**: (i) Q-truncation as an algorithmic novelty for original P2 — knee Q* is asymptotically larger than √h_max in the polylog-h regime; (ii) the hypothesis that σ_HL_Q decreases monotonically with Q across all measured Q (no plateau) — directly REJECTED, clean knee at Q=200/1000-2000; (iii) the hypothesis that σ_HL_Q at Q = max_p_h(h_set) exceeds σ_HL_∞ by > 10% — directly REJECTED, σ_HL_5000 = σ_HL_∞ exactly at 5 decimal places. **What this does NOT close**: (i) conditional theorem rigorising the variance decomposition — slot 4 (4a) target; (ii) third-decade scaling validation at x=10⁹ — slot 4 (4b) candidate; (iii) worst-case (per-h) tail bound — half-Gaussian-shape implies √(log N) worst-case scaling but not formally derived; (iv) effective constant F (slot-2's 0.36-0.70) as part of the named exponent — packaged in (1+o(1)). **Cross-domain ingredient**: same as Goldston-Montgomery 1987 bilinear-form decomposition